.TH SOUND-COMMANDS 1 "2026-07-16" "gway-001" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sound-commands \- local GPIO sound and event notification tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sound
.RI [ sound |list|all|test]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B sound-mode
.RI [ status |silent|on|toggle|test|log|hook-log]
.br
.B gway-event-sound-monitor
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The local sound tools play short GPIO earcons and resolve event-source mappings.
Motifs identify a source before its event sound.
.PP
.B sound
or
.B sound.sh
plays one named pattern directly.
.PP
.B sound-mode
toggles the shared sound-hook silent file and shows recent logs.
.PP
.B gway-event-sound-monitor
watches local host events and sends events directly to the sound engine.
.SH SOUND NAMES
The local vocabulary is:
.TP
.B ok
Single high chirp.
.TP
.B notice
Two even mid chirps.
.TP
.B attention
Rising low-high pair.
.TP
.B warning
Falling high-low pair.
.TP
.B error
Three low buzzes.
.TP
.B busy
Four fast ticks.
.TP
.B critical
Alternating alarm.
.SH SOUND OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --pin " PIN"
BCM GPIO pin. The local default is 18.
.TP
.BI --volume " VALUE"
Volume from 0.0 to 1.0.
.TP
.BI --repeat " COUNT"
Play a sound, event earcon, or custom pattern COUNT times (1 through 20; default 1).
A source motif is announced only once per event invocation.
.TP
.BI --pause " SECONDS"
Delay between repetitions or all/test sounds (0 through 3 seconds; default 0.35).
No delay is added after the final repeat.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print patterns without playing.
.SH SOUND-MODE COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show whether event sounds are audible or silent.
.TP
.B silent
Mute event sounds.
.TP
.B on
Enable event sounds.
.TP
.B toggle
Switch between silent and audible.
.TP
.BI test " SOUND"
Enable sound and play one sound.
.TP
.BI log " N"
Show recent event-sound monitor log lines.
.TP
.BI hook-log " N"
Show recent sound-hook log lines.
.SH EVENT MONITOR OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --poll-seconds " SECONDS"
Polling interval.
.TP
.B --once
Print one snapshot and exit.
.TP
.B --json
Emit JSON with
.BR --once .
.TP
.B --dry-run
Log and print sound decisions without playback.
.SH EXAMPLES
List sound names:
.PP
.nf
sound list
.fi
.PP
Preview all sounds without playing:
.PP
.nf
sound all --dry-run
.fi
.PP
Play the attention sound quietly:
.PP
.nf
sound attention --volume 0.20
.fi
.PP
Repeat the warning earcon three times with a one-second rest:
.PP
.nf
sound warning --repeat 3 --pause 1
.fi
.PP
Mute event sounds:
.PP
.nf
/home/arthe/.local/bin/sound-mode silent
.fi
.PP
Re-enable and test:
.PP
.nf
/home/arthe/.local/bin/sound-mode test ok
.fi
.PP
Run the event monitor once without playback:
.PP
.nf
/home/arthe/.local/bin/gway-event-sound-monitor --once --json --dry-run
.fi
.PP
The GPIO mute toggle marker (normally
.I /run/user/UID/gway-sound/gpio-muted
) suppresses *both* GPIO and audio backends, including motifs and custom
patterns. The legacy Codex hook silent marker also suppresses shared
playback. Mute is checked before each repeat, so muting mid-sequence stops
subsequent repeats. Playback already in progress cannot be interrupted.
Dry-run and resolve modes remain silent inspections regardless of mute.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/sound
GPIO earcon player.
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.local/bin/codex-sound-hook
Deprecated compatibility wrapper for callers not yet migrated.
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.local/state/codex-sound-hooks/silent
Presence of this file mutes both legacy hook and shared sound playback.
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.local/state/codex-sound-hooks/events.log
Sound-hook event log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lcd-commands (1),
.BR rfid-commands (1)

.SH EVENT PLAYBACK
Use sound --event EVENT --source SOURCE for named events.
Use sound --resolve --event EVENT --source SOURCE for a silent JSON lookup.
Mappings are stored in the GWAY sound SQLite event database.
